// =============================================================================
//  WHO Child Growth Standards, LMS by month, birth to 60 months
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  GENERATED 2026-10-02 from the WHO's own published tables
//  (github.com/WorldHealthOrganization/anthro, data-raw/growthstandards:
//  weianthro.txt, lenanthro.txt, hcanthro.txt), which give L, M and S for
//  every day of age. Sampled here at whole months: day = floor(month x
//  30.4375 + 0.5), the WHO's own month length. Do not edit by hand; regenerate.
//
//  L, M, S is how the WHO publishes a skewed distribution in three numbers:
//  M is the median, S the spread, L the skew. For a measurement X:
//      z = ((X / M)^L - 1) / (L * S)        (L != 0)
//  and the value at a z-score is M * (1 + L*S*z)^(1/L). Weight is skewed
//  (L != 1), length and head are not (L = 1), which is why a single
//  "coefficient of variation" was wrong for weight at the edges.
//
//  Length to 24 months is lying down, height after is standing; the WHO
//  table already carries that switch, so nothing here adjusts for it.
// =============================================================================

